KNOWNBUG
member_assignment4.sv
--bound 2
^\[main\.p0\] always \(##1 main\.r == 165\): PROVED up to bound 2$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The value of s after the blocking assignment to s.hi is composed from
the new value of s.hi and, for s.lo, bits extracted from the
struct-typed symbol s. The bit-level layout of a packed struct has the
first member as the most significant, but the extraction is applied to
the struct directly rather than to its bit-vector representation, and
hence yields the bits of the wrong member.
